@startuml
skinparam lifelineStrategy solid
autonumber
title Diagrama Devoluciones 14: GET /api/v1/refunds/approvers?roleCode= (Resolver el rol a personas)

actor "Analista / Gerente" as User
participant "App Web" as Web
participant "Gateway Controller" as Gateway
participant "Refund Workflow Service" as Service
participant "Role Directory Client\n(servicio externo)" as RoleDir
participant "refund_workflow_instance_levels DB" as LevelsDB
participant "refund_workflow_actions DB" as ActionsDB

User -> Web: Abre "¿Quién tiene que firmar?" en el detalle
Web -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/refunds/2001/approvers?roleCode=gerente_cx
Gateway -> Service: getLevelApprovers(refundOrderId: 2001, roleCode, actor)

Service -> LevelsDB: 1. findLevelByRole(instanceId, roleCode)
LevelsDB --> Service: level { id: 201, level_order: 2,\napproval_policy: 'QUORUM', required_approvals: 2 }

Service -> RoleDir: 2. resolveApproversByRole('gerente_cx')
note right of RoleDir
  Nuestras tablas guardan SOLO role_code.
  La lista de personas es del directorio
  externo y puede cambiar entre una consulta
  y la siguiente: no se persiste.
end note
RoleDir --> Service: employees[] (employeeCode, employeeName)

Service -> ActionsDB: 3. findLevelApprovals(instanceId, levelId: 201)
note right of ActionsDB
  Las acciones APPROVE del nivel dicen quién
  ya firmó: actor_employee_code.
end note
ActionsDB --> Service: approvals[]

Service -> Service: 4. computeSignatureState(level, employees, approvals)
note right of Service
  signaturesNeeded:
  - ANY    -> 1
  - ALL    -> cantidad de aprobadores del rol
  - QUORUM -> required_approvals, topeado por
              la cantidad de aprobadores
  Por persona: hasActed (ya firmó) y
  signaturesMissing para el nivel.
end note

Service --> Gateway: 200 OK (LevelApproversResult:\n{ roleCode, approvalPolicy, signaturesNeeded,\nsignaturesReceived, approvers: [{ employeeCode, employeeName, hasActed }] })
Gateway --> Web: 200 OK
Web --> User: Muestra quién firmó y cuántas firmas faltan
@enduml
